**Multidimensional poverty index (0-1)** in 2024 ranges from 0.003 (Nuestra Señora de La Paz) to 0.296 (TIOC-Raqaypampa) across the 343 units with data; the median unit has 0.053.

The 5 highest: TIOC-Raqaypampa (0.296), Poroma (0.223), San Pedro (0.213), El Choro (0.203), Vila Vila (0.2).

The 5 lowest: Nuestra Señora de La Paz (0.003), Colcapirhua (0.005), Trigal (0.006), Santa Cruz de la Sierra (0.006), El Alto (0.006).

The gap between the two ends is 0.293. Extreme values deserve a second look before any analysis: they may be the most interesting units, very small units whose rates are noisy, or errors in the data.

_These are associations, not causal effects. A causal reading needs a research design._
